data: {"done":1,"key":"pcba@th+switch_cord_minor_parts@th","plan":{"move":[{"group":"pcba","to_plant":"th"},{"group":"switch_cord_minor_parts","to_plant":"th"}],"description":"Make PCBA (SMT) and Switch, cord and minor parts in Thailand","variant_facts":"The merchandise under consideration is a Kobalt 12.5-amp heat gun, model 5208257. It features two fan speeds and a variable temperature control dial and is rated at 1500 watts. The main components are a plastic molded housing that encompasses a heating element, motor-fan assembly, power switch and power cord. It delivers hot air for heat shrinking, stripping paint, bending plastic, drying and thawing. The Kobalt 12.5-amp heat gun, model 5208257 is assembled in Thailand using components sourced from Thailand and China.\n\nThe main housing, front cover, heating element, printed circuit board assembly (PCBA), switch, power cord, wiring, knob, back cover and support ring, heat insulator and fasteners are produced in Thailand. The electric motor, fan and motor support are sourced from China. \n\nIn Thailand, the printed circuit board assembly (PCBA) will be produced in-house: SMT placement and reflow of the printed circuit board assembly; test the PCBA.\n\nIn Thailand, the switch, power cord, wiring, knob, back cover and support ring, heat insulator and fasteners will be produced in-house: make the switch, power cord, wiring, supports and fasteners.\n\nFinal assembly in Thailand: press fit the fan to the motor spindle and attach the fan cover; crimp plugs to the heating element wires, add heat shrink tubing, solder wires to the switch and plug the heating element into the switch and PCBA; fasten the PCBA to the main housing, assemble the temperature knob, connect the PCBA to the motor, add the back cover and motor support; secure the power cord, add the switch slider, close the housing with screws, test, label and pack.\n","prediction":{"origin_country":"Thailand","key_factors":["Heating element, PCBA, housing, and final assembly"],"decisive_step":"Manufacturing of the heating element, PCBA (via SMT), and housing, combined with final assembly in Thailand","confidence":0.95,"reasoning":"Similar to N345938, the majority of the components—including the critical heating element, PCBA (fabricated via SMT), switch, power cord, and housing—are manufactured in Thailand. Although the electric motor and fan are sourced from China, the substantive manufacturing of the heat-generating and control components alongside the comprehensive final assembly in Thailand substantially transforms the Chinese components into a new article of commerce.","cited_rulings":["N345938"],"precedents":["N340187","N342124","N345938","N348083","N351922"],"trace":{"llm_provider":"litellm","model_id":"gemini-4-argon","prompt_version":"engine-v1","input_tokens":2773,"output_tokens":193,"latency_ms":1260}},"verdict":{"precedent_supported":true,"supporting_ruling":"N347421","confidence":0.85,"reasoning":"In Variant A, CBP held origin was China (N328954) because although the housing and heating element were made in Thailand and final assembly occurred there, almost all other key functional and structural components (motor, fan, PCBA, switch, power cord, wiring, back cover, insulator) were sourced from China. In Variant B, Thailand manufactures the PCBA via SMT, as well as the switch, power cord, wiring, back cover, insulator, heating element, and housing, leaving only the motor, fan, and support from China. Producing virtually all components (including SMT PCBA and heating element) plus assembly in Thailand confers Thailand origin.","trace":{"llm_provider":"litellm","model_id":"gemini-4-argon","prompt_version":"verifier-v1+known-a","input_tokens":5486,"output_tokens":363,"latency_ms":0}},"duty_effect_per_year":500000,"added_cost_per_year":95000,"net_per_year":405000,"shown":false,"rejection_reason":"precedent-supported but verifier confidence 0.85 is below 0.95","rejection_kind":"below_confidence_bar"},"total":6}

