data: {"done":3,"key":"switch_cord_minor_parts@th","plan":{"move":[{"group":"switch_cord_minor_parts","to_plant":"th"}],"description":"Make Switch, cord and minor parts in Thailand","variant_facts":"The merchandise under consideration is a Kobalt 12.5-amp heat gun, model 5208257. It features two fan speeds and a variable temperature control dial and is rated at 1500 watts. The main components are a plastic molded housing that encompasses a heating element, motor-fan assembly, power switch and power cord. It delivers hot air for heat shrinking, stripping paint, bending plastic, drying and thawing. The Kobalt 12.5-amp heat gun, model 5208257 is assembled in Thailand using components sourced from Thailand and China.\n\nThe main housing, front cover, heating element, switch, power cord, wiring, knob, back cover and support ring, heat insulator and fasteners are produced in Thailand. The electric motor, fan, motor support and printed circuit board assembly (PCBA) are sourced from China. \n\nIn Thailand, the switch, power cord, wiring, knob, back cover and support ring, heat insulator and fasteners will be produced in-house: make the switch, power cord, wiring, supports and fasteners.\n\nFinal assembly in Thailand: press fit the fan to the motor spindle and attach the fan cover; crimp plugs to the heating element wires, add heat shrink tubing, solder wires to the switch and plug the heating element into the switch and PCBA; fasten the PCBA to the main housing, assemble the temperature knob, connect the PCBA to the motor, add the back cover and motor support; secure the power cord, add the switch slider, close the housing with screws, test, label and pack.\n","prediction":{"origin_country":"Thailand","key_factors":["Heating element and housing components"],"decisive_step":"Manufacturing of the heating element, housing, and electrical components, combined with final assembly in Thailand","confidence":0.9,"reasoning":"In Thailand, the critical heating element (which provides the core heat-generating function of a heat gun), the main housing, switch, and power cord are manufactured. Although the motor, fan, and PCBA are sourced from China, the production of the primary heating component and structural housing in Thailand, combined with final assembly, soldering, wiring, and testing in Thailand, constitutes a substantial transformation of the Chinese components into a new and different article of commerce.","cited_rulings":[],"precedents":["N335508","N340187","N342124","N348083","N351782"],"trace":{"llm_provider":"litellm","model_id":"gemini-4-argon","prompt_version":"engine-v1","input_tokens":2827,"output_tokens":186,"latency_ms":678}},"verdict":{"precedent_supported":false,"counter_ruling":"H317645","confidence":0.78,"reasoning":"In Variant A (N328954), CBP held the origin was China even though the main housing, front cover, and heating element were produced in Thailand and final assembly occurred there, because key functional components (electric motor, fan, motor support, PCBA) came from China and final assembly was simple. In Variant B, only minor auxiliary components (switch, power cord, wiring, knob, back cover, insulator, fasteners) shift from China to Thailand, while the core Chinese functional components (motor, fan, motor support, PCBA) and the simple assembly process remain unchanged. Under CBP precedent (e.g., H317645), shifting minor components without changing core assemblies does not alter origin.","trace":{"llm_provider":"litellm","model_id":"gemini-4-argon","prompt_version":"verifier-v1+known-a","input_tokens":7600,"output_tokens":401,"latency_ms":0}},"duty_effect_per_year":500000,"added_cost_per_year":35000,"net_per_year":465000,"shown":false,"rejection_reason":"no earlier ruling found where CBP held this kind of change decisive","rejection_kind":"no_supporting_precedent"},"total":6}

