data: {"done":5,"key":"pcba@th","plan":{"move":[{"group":"pcba","to_plant":"th"}],"description":"Make PCBA (SMT) in Thailand","variant_facts":"The merchandise under consideration is a Kobalt 12.5-amp heat gun, model 5208257. It features two fan speeds and a variable temperature control dial and is rated at 1500 watts. The main components are a plastic molded housing that encompasses a heating element, motor-fan assembly, power switch and power cord. It delivers hot air for heat shrinking, stripping paint, bending plastic, drying and thawing. The Kobalt 12.5-amp heat gun, model 5208257 is assembled in Thailand using components sourced from Thailand and China.\n\nThe main housing, front cover, heating element and printed circuit board assembly (PCBA) are produced in Thailand. The electric motor, fan, motor support, switch, power cord, wiring, knob, back cover and support ring, heat insulator and fasteners are sourced from China. \n\nIn Thailand, the printed circuit board assembly (PCBA) will be produced in-house: SMT placement and reflow of the printed circuit board assembly; test the PCBA.\n\nFinal assembly in Thailand: press fit the fan to the motor spindle and attach the fan cover; crimp plugs to the heating element wires, add heat shrink tubing, solder wires to the switch and plug the heating element into the switch and PCBA; fasten the PCBA to the main housing, assemble the temperature knob, connect the PCBA to the motor, add the back cover and motor support; secure the power cord, add the switch slider, close the housing with screws, test, label and pack.\n","prediction":{"origin_country":"Thailand","key_factors":["Heating element and Printed Circuit Board Assembly (PCBA)"],"decisive_step":"Production of the heating element and PCBA (via SMT), combined with final assembly in Thailand","confidence":0.92,"reasoning":"Consistent with N345938 and N348083, the origin of an electro-thermal appliance is driven by its core functional components and complex manufacturing. Here, the heating element (which provides the primary heat-generating function), the PCBA (manufactured via SMT to control temperature and fan speed), and the main housing are all produced in Thailand. Combining these critical Thai-origin components with the Chinese motor and fan via soldering, wiring, and mechanical assembly in Thailand substantially transforms the parts into a heat gun of Thai origin.","cited_rulings":["N348083","N345938"],"precedents":["N340187","N342124","N345938","N348083","N351922"],"trace":{"llm_provider":"litellm","model_id":"gemini-4-argon","prompt_version":"engine-v1","input_tokens":2730,"output_tokens":229,"latency_ms":752}},"verdict":{"precedent_supported":false,"counter_ruling":"H309758","confidence":0.65,"reasoning":"In Variant A (N328954), CBP held the heat gun's origin is China despite the main housing, front cover, heating element, and final assembly being in Thailand, because the electric motor, fan, PCBA, switch, and other components come from China. Moving only the PCBA (SMT placement and reflow) to Thailand in Variant B leaves the Chinese electric motor, fan, motor support, switch, power cord, and other components unchanged. As examined in H309758 (comparing Scenario 1 vs. Scenario 2 for a heating tool where PCBA population shifts to the assembly country), shifting a control PCBA alone does not alter origin when core functional components remain Chinese.","trace":{"llm_provider":"litellm","model_id":"gemini-4-argon","prompt_version":"verifier-v1+known-a","input_tokens":9131,"output_tokens":474,"latency_ms":0}},"duty_effect_per_year":500000,"added_cost_per_year":60000,"net_per_year":440000,"shown":false,"rejection_reason":"no earlier ruling found where CBP held this kind of change decisive","rejection_kind":"no_supporting_precedent"},"total":6}

