data: {"done":6,"key":"motor_fan_assembly@th+pcba@th","plan":{"move":[{"group":"motor_fan_assembly","to_plant":"th"},{"group":"pcba","to_plant":"th"}],"description":"Make Motor-fan assembly and PCBA (SMT) in Thailand","variant_facts":"The merchandise under consideration is a Kobalt 12.5-amp heat gun, model 5208257. It features two fan speeds and a variable temperature control dial and is rated at 1500 watts. The main components are a plastic molded housing that encompasses a heating element, motor-fan assembly, power switch and power cord. It delivers hot air for heat shrinking, stripping paint, bending plastic, drying and thawing. The Kobalt 12.5-amp heat gun, model 5208257 is assembled in Thailand using components sourced from Thailand and China.\n\nThe main housing, front cover, heating element, electric motor, fan, motor support and printed circuit board assembly (PCBA) are produced in Thailand. The switch, power cord, wiring, knob, back cover and support ring, heat insulator and fasteners are sourced from China. \n\nIn Thailand, the electric motor, fan and motor support will be produced in-house: stamp rotor laminations from silicon steel; stack laminations and wind the rotor; build the stator; assemble the motor; press-fit the fan to the motor spindle.\n\nIn Thailand, the printed circuit board assembly (PCBA) will be produced in-house: SMT placement and reflow of the printed circuit board assembly; test the PCBA.\n\nFinal assembly in Thailand: press fit the fan to the motor spindle and attach the fan cover; crimp plugs to the heating element wires, add heat shrink tubing, solder wires to the switch and plug the heating element into the switch and PCBA; fasten the PCBA to the main housing, assemble the temperature knob, connect the PCBA to the motor, add the back cover and motor support; secure the power cord, add the switch slider, close the housing with screws, test, label and pack.\n","prediction":{"origin_country":"Thailand","key_factors":["Heating element, electric motor-fan assembly, and PCBA"],"decisive_step":"In-house manufacturing of the electric motor (stamping, winding), PCBA (SMT), heating element, and housing, plus final assembly in Thailand","confidence":0.98,"reasoning":"The components that impart the essential character of the heat gun—the heating element, electric motor, fan, PCBA, and main housing—are all manufactured in Thailand through substantial operations including silicon steel stamping, rotor winding, and SMT placement. As in N342124 and N345938, fabricating the core functional subassemblies and performing final assembly in Thailand substantially transforms the minor Chinese components (switch, cord, wiring, fasteners) into a new article of commerce of Thai origin.","cited_rulings":["N342124","N345938"],"precedents":["N340187","N342124","N345938","N348083","N351922"],"trace":{"llm_provider":"litellm","model_id":"gemini-4-argon","prompt_version":"engine-v1","input_tokens":2783,"output_tokens":241,"latency_ms":1319}},"verdict":{"precedent_supported":true,"supporting_ruling":"N347421","counter_ruling":"N345859","confidence":0.92,"reasoning":"In N347421 and N345859 (fan-forced electric heaters), CBP held that the heating element, electric motor, fan, and control components impart the essential identity and functionality of a hot-air appliance. In Variant A, the motor, fan, and PCBA are sourced from China, leaving China as the origin despite Thai heating element and housing production. In Variant B, manufacturing the electric motor (stamping laminations, winding rotor, building stator), fan, and PCBA (SMT placement and reflow) in Thailand—alongside the Thai heating element, main housing, and final assembly—means all essential functional components originate in Thailand, shifting origin to Thailand as in N347421.","trace":{"llm_provider":"litellm","model_id":"gemini-4-argon","prompt_version":"verifier-v1+known-a","input_tokens":12461,"output_tokens":736,"latency_ms":0}},"duty_effect_per_year":500000,"added_cost_per_year":180000,"net_per_year":320000,"shown":false,"rejection_reason":"precedent-supported but verifier confidence 0.92 is below 0.95","rejection_kind":"below_confidence_bar"},"total":6}

